AWS Services
Service	            Purpose
Amazon S3	            Stores source and processed images
AWS Lambda	            Processes uploaded images
CloudWatch Logs	      Stores Lambda execution logs
CloudWatch Metrics	Provides built-in and custom application metrics
CloudWatch Alarms	      Detects abnormal conditions
CloudWatch Dashboard	Visualizes application health
Amazon SNS	            Sends alarm notifications


Monitoring

Built-in Lambda Metrics :
Metric	Purpose	Alarm
Invocations	Number of Lambda executions	≥ 5
Errors	Number of failed executions	≥ 2
Throttles	Number of throttled invocation requests	≥ 2

Custom Metrics :
Metric	Source Log Event	Purpose
ImageProcessingSuccess	PNG uploaded successfully	Tracks successful image processing
ImageProcessingTimeout	Status: timeout	Tracks application timeouts

Custom metrics are created using CloudWatch Log Metric Filters.

SNS Notifications

CloudWatch alarms publish notifications to an SNS topic.

Notifications are configured for:

Alarm state
OK/recovery state

This provides immediate visibility when the Lambda crosses a configured threshold and when it returns to normal.

